{"title":"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 29","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given the three numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/b/2fbd92b8fc1d1edfd257b9aa7dea1b88a226c447.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y=x^x,z=x^{x^x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"136\" height=\"19\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/a/1fa892c25e4d956c369b338c9b46242595da474a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$.9&lt;x&lt;1.0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"95\" height=\"13\" />. Arranged in order of increasing magnitude, they are:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8ea1e9b70678b755ab38490a7bf23f7140fbd64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } x,z,y\\quad \\text{(B) } x,y,z\\quad \\text{(C) } y,x,z\\quad \\text{(D) } y,z,x\\quad \\text{(E) } z,x,y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"445\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Seeing that we need to compare values with exponents, we think <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logarithms\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Logarithms\">logarithms</a>. Taking the logarithm base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> of each term, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/1/0c112df2a51295df3c201e3c9caf96a2f9b8d413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^x$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/8/128206b7583760e7ef76e802861294c334f7ca2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;x&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/e/9bec46dc3f02fd374a60a65a994b47ef3cf1c2ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)=\\log_x(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" /> is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Monotonic\" title=\"Monotonic\">monotonically decreasing</a>, so the order of terms by magnitude in our new set of numbers will be reversed compared to the original set (i.e. if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/a/5ba70df5a2f9630194f32f50010cd2e78318c98d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;b&lt;c$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/3/ae3a37be709ef66b3972b26893aa7562398d39eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_x(a)&gt;\\log_x(b)&gt;\\log_x(c))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"221\" height=\"20\" />. However, the order of this set will be reversed again (back to the order of the original set) when we take the logarithm base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> a second time. After doing this operation, we find the values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, which correspond to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, respectively. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/8/fc897d766190b8eedd59350adf73b94e98e8b571.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.9&lt;x&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/8/128206b7583760e7ef76e802861294c334f7ca2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;x&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" />, and so, by the correspondence detailed above, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/0/42053d8c09f965847ff3fed6831ae76012a91fdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;z&lt;y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" />, which yields us answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/386255c1da145bc497cf598169ccbaa210e8d0cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/8/128206b7583760e7ef76e802861294c334f7ca2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;x&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" />, taking <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />th power will bring it closer to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, thereby raising its value. Because we have established that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/7/d07a9cd14cf9921f3c1fdba9d6f71566cfde02ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;x^x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/5/d05aa6d8a915a41b9d1786b1d5cc435ee233a1b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)=x^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Monotonic\" title=\"Monotonic\">monotonically decreasing</a> function, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/7/eb791c86e00b13fd02cce0ba82e8c7d5d96edc44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^x&gt;x^{x^x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"71\" height=\"19\" />. However, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/7/a570d62423f06e50b16b914fafc9f91f84b77931.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^x&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/d/8bd1716f48e029c358d69c5d1058c2f0e4cbe40c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{x^x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" />, compared to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, will be closer to (but still less than) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/c/28c366cac34e31f04a78be3af2ead4b362fea346.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{x^x}&gt;x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"19\" />. Putting this all together, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/a/fba4e715795991f51bd4a65a2b6d69350b02a98d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;x^{x^x}&lt;x^x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"106\" height=\"19\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/0/42053d8c09f965847ff3fed6831ae76012a91fdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;z&lt;y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" />, which is answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/386255c1da145bc497cf598169ccbaa210e8d0cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME\" title=\"1968 AHSME\">1968 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1968 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1968\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">Problem 28</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">Problem 30</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 25\">25</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">26</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">27</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">28</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">29</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">30</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_31\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 31\">31</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 32\">32</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_33\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 33\">33</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_34\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 34\">34</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_35\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 35\">35</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AHSME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AHSME Problems and Solutions\"> All AHSME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017165700\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.065 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 306/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2746/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 176/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6641/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.026      1 -total\n 61.62%    8.643      1 Template:AHSME_35p_box\n 36.25%    5.085      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:13018:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017165700 and revision id 222947. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}